rently does not provide `Eq`, `Hash`, or"},{"DocComment":" access to the raw value. This type does provide `PartialEq` for"},{"DocComment":" comparison, but note that there may potentially be multiple failure"},{"DocComment":" codes, some of which will _not_ compare equal to `ExitCode::FAILURE`."},{"DocComment":" The standard library provides the canonical `SUCCESS` and `FAILURE`"},{"DocComment":" exit codes as well as `From<u8> for ExitCode` for constructing other"},{"DocComment":" arbitrary exit codes."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Portability"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Numeric values used in this type don't have portable meanings, and"},{"DocComment":" different platforms may mask different amounts of them."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" For the platform's canonical successful and unsuccessful codes, see"},{"DocComment":" the [`SUCCESS`] and [`FAILURE`] associated items."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`SUCCESS`]: ExitCode::SUCCESS"},{"DocComment":" [`FAILURE`]: ExitCode::FAILURE"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Differences from `ExitStatus`"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" `ExitCode` is intended for terminating the currently running process, via"},{"DocComment":" the `Termination` trait, in contrast to [`ExitStatus`], which represents the"},{"DocComment":" termination of a child process. These APIs are separate due to platform"},{"DocComment":" compatibility differences and their expected usage; it is not generally"},{"DocComment":" possible to exactly reproduce an `ExitStatus` from a child for the current"},{"DocComment":" process after the fact."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" `ExitCode` can be returned from the `main` function of a crate, as it implements"},{"DocComment":" [`Termination`]:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" use std::process::ExitCode;"},{"DocComment":" # fn check_foo() -> bool { true }"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" fn main() -> E